---
description: Opening a pull request against Godlint
alwaysApply: false
---

Read `CONTRIBUTING.md` in full — branch prefix, template choice, and what the two drift labels
mean. `validate-pull-request.py`'s change-scoped checks measure against the release line, not the
branch's own target, so a stack of pull requests needs one changelog entry for the whole change.
Most labels apply automatically from the paths touched; only the two drift labels
(`fixes-false-positive` / `relaxes-a-rule`) are ever applied by hand.
